{
    "background_story": "Kabir was a young monk who lived in a serene monastery nestled in the Himalayas. Every morning, he would wake up before dawn to meditate and practice yoga on the rooftop, watching the sun rise over the mountains. The stillness of the morning air and the gentle warmth of the sunrise invigorated his spirit, preparing him for a day of contemplation and service. As the monastery's resident poet, Kabir would often compose verses during these morning hours, inspired by the beauty of nature and the tranquility of the morning. His poetry, infused with the essence of the morning, became renowned for its soothing quality, calming the minds and hearts of all who read it. Kabir's love for the morning hours was contagious, and soon the entire monastery adopted his habit of rising early to greet the dawn.",
